<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/dreyfus-affair" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dreyfus-affair.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-5">5 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Alfred Dreyfus is publicly stripped of his rank in Paris</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus">Alfred Dreyfus</a>, wrongly convicted of treason in December 1894, was degraded at the Military School in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>: his badges were torn off and his sword broken. Still protesting his innocence, he was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devils-island">Devil's Island</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dreyfus-affair">Dreyfus Affair</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus">Alfred Dreyfus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devils-island">Devil's Island</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pretoria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-1">1 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Paul Kruger proclaims Fountains Valley in Pretoria a nature reserve</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-kruger">Paul Kruger</a> proclaimed the Fountains Valley, at the southern entrance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a>, a nature reserve. This 60 ha reserve and the neighbouring Groenkloof Nature Reserve are the oldest nature reserves on the African continent.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-kruger">Paul Kruger</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-22">22 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lumière brothers show their first film</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At a meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, Louis and Auguste Lumière projected 'Workers Leaving the Lumière Factory' with their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinematograph">Cinématographe</a>. Their first paying public screening followed in December.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-17">17 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Shimonoseki ends the First Sino-Japanese War</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> recognised Korean independence, ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penghu">Pescadores</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and paid a large indemnity. Defeat exposed the weakness of the Qing and announced Japan as a regional power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-8">8 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Wilhelm Röntgen discovers X-rays</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Experimenting with a cathode-ray tube in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-rontgen">Wilhelm Röntgen</a> noticed a glowing screen across the room and identified a new penetrating radiation. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/x-ray">X-rays</a> transformed medicine and won him the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Physics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-28">28 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Lumière brothers hold the first paid public film screening</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Grand Café in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, Auguste and Louis Lumière projected ten short films to a paying audience. The screening is often taken as the birth of cinema.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/triple-intervention" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/triple-intervention.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/triple-intervention">Triple Intervention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Triple Intervention was the diplomatic intervention of Russia, Germany and France on 23 April 1895, six days after the Treaty of Shimonoseki ended the First Sino-Japanese War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-revolution-of-1895" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liberal-revolution-of-1895.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/liberal-revolution-of-1895">Liberal Revolution of 1895</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Liberal Revolution of 1895 in Ecuador began with a rising in Guayaquil on 5 June 1895 that proclaimed Eloy Alfaro supreme chief.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/akassa-raid">Akassa raid</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Akassa raid was an attack on 29 January 1895 by warriors of the Nembe kingdom of Brass, led by King Frederick William Koko, on the Royal Niger Company's depot at Akassa in the Niger delta.</p></div></li></ol></section>
